1
00:00:03,008 --> 00:00:04,723
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:04,801 --> 00:00:06,342
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:06,533 --> 00:00:12,062
اَلْحَمْدُ لله  وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:14,168 --> 00:00:22,139
Rasool Allah ﷺ was delivering a Khut'ba(خطبة), and he said;

5
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:35,715
إنَّ الله خيرا عبدًا مِن عباده بين الدنيا وبين ما عندالله فختارا ذالك العبد ما عندالله

6
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:48,110
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has given one of His slaves, two choices.

7
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:53,768
The first choice is to stay in this world.

8
00:00:55,332 --> 00:00:59,578
The second choice is to leave to die

9
00:01:00,942 --> 00:01:05,737
and to go to what Allah سبحانه وتعالى has for that person in the afterlife

10
00:01:07,836 --> 00:01:11,653
and that slave has chosen the latter.

11
00:01:12,286 --> 00:01:18,098
That slave has chosen to go to what Allah has reserved for him in the afterlife.

12
00:01:21,392 --> 00:01:23,672
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه started crying.

13
00:01:25,048 --> 00:01:27,328
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبوسعيدألخدري) one of the Ansaar(أنْصَار). He said:

14
00:01:27,368 --> 00:01:31,217
We looked at Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) and we couldn't figure out, why he is crying.

15
00:01:33,771 --> 00:01:37,129
It doesn't seem to be something very emotional about that statement.

16
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:43,895
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has given one of His slaves, the choice of staying in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) or leaving Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

17
00:01:44,316 --> 00:01:46,792
 given him the choice of living longer, or dying.

18
00:01:47,579 --> 00:01:49,784
So, why is Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) crying?

19
00:01:52,272 --> 00:01:53,741
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبوسعيدألخدري) said;

20
00:01:55,078 --> 00:01:56,939
But then we came to know why he cried

21
00:01:57,729 --> 00:02:00,968
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was the only one among us

22
00:02:01,273 --> 00:02:04,129
who understood what Rasool Allah ﷺ meant.

23
00:02:04,943 --> 00:02:07,582
Rasool Allah ﷺ was actually talking about himself.

24
00:02:08,483 --> 00:02:09,970
He was that slave of Allah.

25
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:20,055
But you see Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه because of the fact that he has spent so much time with Rasool Allah ﷺ

26
00:02:20,333 --> 00:02:22,730
more than anyone else among the Sahabah(صحابه)

27
00:02:23,618 --> 00:02:27,892
 he could understand Rasool Allah ﷺ better and more than anybody else.

28
00:02:29,282 --> 00:02:33,586
And he can get the message sometimes without Rasool Allah ﷺ even speaking it

29
00:02:35,241 --> 00:02:38,594
because they have been friends for their entire lives.

30
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:45,558
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was weeping, and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said the following,

31
00:02:46,562 --> 00:02:55,900
إنَّ أمنَّ الناس عليَّ في صحبته ، وماله أبوبكر

32
00:02:58,972 --> 00:03:03,852
The one, who has done me, the greatest favors

33
00:03:04,563 --> 00:03:09,575
through his friendship to me, and his wealth, is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

34
00:03:12,164 --> 00:03:17,302
Now imagine Rasool Allah ﷺ saying this towards the end of his life in front of all of the Sahabah(صحابه)

35
00:03:17,807 --> 00:03:24,533
an admission, a recognition of his close friend and companion, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

36
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:28,178
He is saying that he has done me so many favors.

37
00:03:28,983 --> 00:03:31,590
In fact another Hadith(حديث),  Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

38
00:03:33,177 --> 00:03:38,424
Every one of you, who has done me a favor, I have paid them back except Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

39
00:03:41,377 --> 00:03:42,876
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

40
00:03:44,364 --> 00:03:53,122
ولو كنت متخذً خليلً غير ربي لتخذت ابابكر خليل

41
00:03:56,626 --> 00:04:07,441
ولكن أخوة الإسلام ومودة لا يبقين في المسجد باب إلَّا سدَّا إلَّا باب أبي بكرٍ رواه البخاري

42
00:04:07,465 --> 00:04:11,700
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: And if I were to take a Khalil(خليل)

43
00:04:11,724 --> 00:04:14,519
a Khalil(خليل) is something higher than a Sahib(صاحب), a Sahib(صاحب) is a friend

44
00:04:15,062 --> 00:04:17,712
Khalil(خليل) is a higher level of friendship, very close.

45
00:04:18,066 --> 00:04:23,679
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If I was to take a Khalil(خليل) besides Allah

46
00:04:24,603 --> 00:04:26,128
it would be Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

47
00:04:27,148 --> 00:04:29,560
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that I'm the Khalil(خليل) of Allah

48
00:04:30,255 --> 00:04:32,753
that he is the Khalil(خليل) of Allah.

49
00:04:32,777 --> 00:04:34,338
Rasool Allah ﷺ is the Khalil(خليل) of Allah.

50
00:04:34,695 --> 00:04:35,774
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

51
00:04:35,972 --> 00:04:40,489
If I were to be a Khalil(خليل) of someone else, it would be Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

52
00:04:40,929 --> 00:04:42,988
but between us is Akhuwat-Tul-Islam(أخوة الإسلام)

53
00:04:43,214 --> 00:04:47,729
the brotherhood of Islam Wa-Muwaddato(ومودةُ) and the love of Islam.

54
00:04:48,313 --> 00:04:50,324
That's the relationship between me and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

55
00:04:51,051 --> 00:04:53,851
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said, you know, in the Masjid-e-Nabawi(مسجد النبوي).

56
00:04:55,609 --> 00:05:02,766
The Sahabah(صحابه), particularly the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) they were given small pieces of land next to the Masjid(مسجد).

57
00:05:03,955 --> 00:05:10,649
So they would build their houses, right next to the walls of Masjid-e-Nabawi(مسجد النبوي)

58
00:05:11,431 --> 00:05:14,405
and they would open for themselves very small gates

59
00:05:14,544 --> 00:05:17,625
so that they could immediately walk from their house to the Masjid(مسجد).

60
00:05:18,319 --> 00:05:21,278
So, these were private doors of some of the Sahabah(صحابه)

61
00:05:21,647 --> 00:05:24,229
and there are quite a few of them, Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

62
00:05:25,471 --> 00:05:31,625
And I want all of these private doors to be closed except for the door of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

63
00:05:32,912 --> 00:05:36,518
That's the privilege that only goes to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

64
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:39,809
the one who will have a private entrance into Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi(ألمسجد النبوي).

65
00:05:40,267 --> 00:05:43,667
Imagine having your private gate, no one gets in except you.

66
00:05:44,963 --> 00:05:47,320
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: All of them should be closed

67
00:05:47,543 --> 00:05:48,960
except the gate of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

68
00:05:51,583 --> 00:05:52,696
and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

69
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:59,351
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه got the message that Rasool Allah ﷺ is towards the end of his life.

70
00:06:00,432 --> 00:06:01,852
Rasool Allah ﷺ became ill

71
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:05,863
that was a few months after he came back from Hajjat-Ul-Widaa(حجة الوداع).

72
00:06:09,875 --> 00:06:14,979
Rasool Allah ﷺ, his illness was getting worse and worse

73
00:06:16,689 --> 00:06:19,070
and he was unable to join in Salaat-Ul-Jama'at(صلوات الجماعة).

74
00:06:19,382 --> 00:06:20,243
So he said:

75
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:24,485
مُرُوا أبَا بَكْرٍ أنْ يُصَلِّيَ بالنَّاسِ،

76
00:06:25,497 --> 00:06:29,036
Instruct Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be the Imam(اِمَام), in Salah(صلاة).

77
00:06:30,913 --> 00:06:37,351
Ayesha رضي الله عنها when she heard that she was trying to change the mind of Muhammadﷺ.

78
00:06:37,827 --> 00:06:38,593
She said;

79
00:06:39,438 --> 00:06:41,019
إنَّ أبي رجلٌ أصيف

80
00:06:41,043 --> 00:06:42,854
My father is very soft hearted

81
00:06:43,858 --> 00:06:46,354
and if he stands in your place, he will break down.

82
00:06:47,009 --> 00:06:50,031
It's not easy to be standing in the same place of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

83
00:06:51,043 --> 00:06:55,026
She said: If he stands in that position, He might break down, he's very soft hearted.

84
00:06:56,554 --> 00:06:59,763
So, why don't you tell Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to take that position.

85
00:07:01,616 --> 00:07:08,442
In reality, Ayesha رضي الله عنها also had another reason for not wanting her father to be there

86
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:11,715
to give you an example to draw the point closer.

87
00:07:12,139 --> 00:07:16,332
Imagine that you came a very long distance to hear Khut'ba(خطبة) from a very well known scholar.

88
00:07:17,082 --> 00:07:20,910
There's an ad that says that this very well known scholar is coming into town

89
00:07:21,037 --> 00:07:22,235
and he's going to give Khut'ba(خطبة).

90
00:07:22,390 --> 00:07:25,261
So you come from all over London to attend this Khut'ba(خطبة).

91
00:07:25,877 --> 00:07:30,292
And then you come there, and we find that it's not this scholar you came to hear, its someone else

92
00:07:31,472 --> 00:07:32,501
you're not gonna like that.

93
00:07:35,552 --> 00:07:40,645
Ayesha رضي الله عنها was thinking that this is a place where the people are expecting Rasool Allah ﷺ to be.

94
00:07:41,049 --> 00:07:44,452
So when they see my father, they're not gonna like that.

95
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:48,293
They're used to Rasool Allah ﷺ leading them that position.

96
00:07:48,694 --> 00:07:51,183
So she wanted to change the mind of Rasool Allah ﷺ, she said;

97
00:07:51,449 --> 00:07:52,541
Why don't you have Umar(عُمَر) do it?

98
00:07:53,874 --> 00:07:54,874
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

99
00:07:55,012 --> 00:07:56,791
مُرُوا أبَا بَكْرٍ أنْ يُصَلِّيَ بالنَّاسِ،

100
00:07:57,097 --> 00:07:58,673
Instruct Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be the Imam(اِمَام)

101
00:07:59,764 --> 00:08:07,023
She again suggested otherwise, Rasool Allah ﷺ the third time said;

102
00:08:07,047 --> 00:08:09,512
إنَّكُنَّ لَأَنْتُنَّ صَوَاحِبُات يُوسُفَ،

103
00:08:09,962 --> 00:08:11,886
You're like the woman of Yousuf(يوسف)

104
00:08:12,247 --> 00:08:14,001
tell Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the people in Salah(صلاة).

105
00:08:14,402 --> 00:08:16,687
What Rasool Allah ﷺ meant by the woman of Yousuf(يوسف)?

106
00:08:17,096 --> 00:08:24,025
The woman of Yousuf(يوسف) they showed something they didn't really mean they had a different motive.

107
00:08:24,631 --> 00:08:30,762
So Rasool Allah ﷺ felt that there is a different motive here why she doesn't want her father to be the Imam(اِمَام).

108
00:08:34,707 --> 00:08:38,736
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه became the Imam(اِمَام) of the Muslims for a few days,

109
00:08:39,079 --> 00:08:41,055
he was leading them in Salah(صلاة).

110
00:08:42,164 --> 00:08:44,387
And by the way, Abul Hasan Al-Ash'ari(أبوالحسن ألأشعري)

111
00:08:45,637 --> 00:08:50,707
he uses this as an evidence that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is the greatest scholar in this Ummah(امة),

112
00:08:51,986 --> 00:08:55,420
 he says because Rasool Allah ﷺ says that the one, who should lead the Salah(صلاة)

113
00:08:56,021 --> 00:08:58,655
is the one, who has most knowledge in the book of Allah.

114
00:09:00,375 --> 00:09:03,027
So since Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was told to lead the Muslims in Salah(صلاة)

115
00:09:03,067 --> 00:09:06,334
it's not just because he's the friend of Rasool Allah ﷺ and he is close companion

116
00:09:06,358 --> 00:09:07,988
 but also because he has the most Fiqh(فقه).

117
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:12,841
The deepest knowledge in Islam or understanding in Islam

118
00:09:13,225 --> 00:09:16,909
and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he comments on these words of Abul Hasan Al-Ash'ari(أبوالحسن ألأشعري) and says;

119
00:09:17,084 --> 00:09:19,148
 This should be written in letters of gold.

120
00:09:19,667 --> 00:09:26,753
They're very valuable words in proving that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is in fact the most scholarly person in this Ummah(امة).

121
00:09:29,412 --> 00:09:32,615
One day Rasool Allah ﷺ felt better.

122
00:09:33,027 --> 00:09:40,934
He was still very exhausted and Rasool Allah ﷺ was once touched by Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله إبن مسعود).

123
00:09:42,108 --> 00:09:47,663
So he saw that the temperature of Rasool Allah ﷺ was very high so he said:

124
00:09:48,241 --> 00:09:51,059
O Messenger of Allah, you have a very strong fever.

125
00:09:51,686 --> 00:09:58,868
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! We the prophets, our fever is double the fever of everyone else.

126
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,502
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

127
00:10:02,596 --> 00:10:06,101
أشدُّ النَّاسِ بلاءً ، الأنبياءُ ، فا الأمثلُ فالأمثلُ ،

128
00:10:06,446 --> 00:10:09,536
The people, who go through the most severe tests are the Prophets

129
00:10:10,699 --> 00:10:13,072
and then it goes down, according to your level.

130
00:10:13,877 --> 00:10:18,556
So the greater a person is and the closer they are to Allah, the more difficult the test would be.

131
00:10:19,505 --> 00:10:20,998
Just like when you take an exam

132
00:10:22,241 --> 00:10:25,361
there are some questions that only an A student would be able to handle

133
00:10:25,572 --> 00:10:27,097
not everybody else would be able to handle them.

134
00:10:27,573 --> 00:10:30,891
And there are some questions who're only the A plus could answer

135
00:10:30,915 --> 00:10:32,626
because these are very difficult questions.

136
00:10:33,614 --> 00:10:36,981
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ puts the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) through some very difficult tests.

137
00:10:40,631 --> 00:10:42,140
Now the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) said;

138
00:10:42,204 --> 00:10:50,108
And I could see Rasool Allah ﷺ being carried by two men Al-Abbas(العباس) and Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

139
00:10:50,604 --> 00:10:53,292
وقدماه تخطان في الأرض

140
00:10:53,317 --> 00:11:00,028
And his feet are dragging on the ground that was how ill Rasool Allah ﷺ was he can't even move his feet

141
00:11:00,085 --> 00:11:03,631
 and he is carried by the two companions, رضي الله عنهم.

142
00:11:05,362 --> 00:11:06,482
They already started the Salah(صلاة).

143
00:11:08,771 --> 00:11:12,757
So when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه saw Rasool Allah ﷺ coming he retreated

144
00:11:12,932 --> 00:11:14,153
he wanted to go back.

145
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:18,562
Rasool Allah ﷺ waved to him and told him to stay where you are

146
00:11:19,207 --> 00:11:21,915
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ came and sat next to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

147
00:11:22,355 --> 00:11:24,209
and he started leading him in Salah(صلاة).

148
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:26,796
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is following Rasool Allah ﷺ

149
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:29,238
and the Sahabah(صحابه) are following Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

150
00:11:32,163 --> 00:11:34,809
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ went back again.

151
00:11:37,673 --> 00:11:42,443
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه carried on leading the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) in Salah(صلاة),

152
00:11:42,562 --> 00:11:46,861
 until it was Monday the 12 of Rabiul-Awwal(ربيع الأول).

153
00:11:48,973 --> 00:12:00,089
In Salaat-Ul-Fajr(صلاةالافجر) Rasool Allah ﷺ opened his curtain and he was standing,

154
00:12:00,792 --> 00:12:02,860
and he took a look at the Sahabah(صحابه) in Salah(صلاة)

155
00:12:04,049 --> 00:12:07,964
the room of Ayesha(عائشه) was right there, touching the Masjid(مسجد).

156
00:12:08,555 --> 00:12:11,930
So the only thing separating the room from the Masjid(مسجد) was a curtain.

157
00:12:12,974 --> 00:12:14,944
Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered that curtain

158
00:12:15,472 --> 00:12:18,498
and he took a look at the Sahabah(صحابه) praying in Salaat-Ul-Fajr(صلاةالافجر)

159
00:12:19,612 --> 00:12:24,867
the Masjid(مسجد) is full and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is reciting Qur'an in Salah(صلاة).

160
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:32,330
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that he smiled and you could see happiness in his face

161
00:12:32,565 --> 00:12:34,568
so the narrator of the Hadith(حديث) said;

162
00:12:35,425 --> 00:12:38,652
The face of Rasool Allah ﷺ became like a plate of silver,

163
00:12:40,053 --> 00:12:42,862
it was shining with light.

164
00:12:43,545 --> 00:12:51,694
Rasool Allah ﷺ was so happy because Rasool Allah ﷺ was now seeing the fruit of his harvest.

165
00:12:52,654 --> 00:12:56,290
He is seeing the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, performing the Salah(صلاة)

166
00:12:56,554 --> 00:12:58,198
the greatest duty in Islam.

167
00:12:59,115 --> 00:13:03,276
So Rasool Allah ﷺ was seeing with his own eyes the success of his message.

168
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:07,797
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the most successful of all of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah

169
00:13:08,713 --> 00:13:13,410
with other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), when they pass away their Ummah(امة) cannot carry on after them.

170
00:13:14,311 --> 00:13:19,331
They go down, down, down, until they reached to the bottom

171
00:13:19,866 --> 00:13:22,851
and then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has to send another Nabi(نَبِي) to bring them up.

172
00:13:23,371 --> 00:13:28,801
With Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) at a particular time they had 70 Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) at one moment,

173
00:13:29,678 --> 00:13:31,171
 to keep them on the straight path

174
00:13:32,059 --> 00:13:39,074
but Rasool Allah ﷺ has succeeded in his message so well to the extent that there's no need for a prophet after him

175
00:13:40,551 --> 00:13:44,205
and his students are so successful. As Allah سبحانه وتعالى said;

176
00:13:44,229 --> 00:13:46,086
كُنتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ

177
00:13:46,288 --> 00:13:49,082
You're the best Ummah(امة) brought forth for mankind

178
00:13:49,325 --> 00:13:55,818
that they will carry on with His message, carrying the banner of Islam until the day of judgment.

179
00:13:56,694 --> 00:13:57,905
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

180
00:13:58,076 --> 00:14:00,295
لا تَزالُ طائفةٌ مِن أُمَّتي على الحقِّ

181
00:14:00,665 --> 00:14:04,674
There will remain a group of my Ummah(امة) on straight path until the day of judgment,

182
00:14:04,809 --> 00:14:06,516
 until they end up fighting with Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال).

183
00:14:08,361 --> 00:14:10,321
So Rasool Allah ﷺ was so happy

184
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:14,193
that he felt now he is ready to leave, his mission is completed.

185
00:14:16,007 --> 00:14:19,162
He can entrust the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم with the responsibility

186
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:23,226
with appointing their own leader, with carrying on the message of Islam.

187
00:14:24,262 --> 00:14:28,617
And that's why the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ was shining and he was smiling and so happy.

188
00:14:30,316 --> 00:14:31,212
As-Sahabi(صحابي) said:

189
00:14:31,236 --> 00:14:33,586
وَكِدنا نُفتَنُ عن صلاتِنا

190
00:14:33,907 --> 00:14:36,392
When we saw Rasool Allah ﷺ, when we saw his face

191
00:14:36,737 --> 00:14:38,989
we were about to forget about our Salah(صلاة).

192
00:14:39,873 --> 00:14:44,408
It was such an emotional thing for us, we were about to forget our Salah(صلاة)

193
00:14:44,554 --> 00:14:45,649
نُفتَنُ عن صلاتِنا

194
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:48,596
It was going to be a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for us in our Salah(صلاة).

195
00:14:51,642 --> 00:14:54,897
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after he completed the Salah(صلاة)

196
00:14:54,922 --> 00:14:57,311
he went to his daughter Ayesha رضي الله عنها and said;

197
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,613
It seems that Rasool Allah ﷺ is getting better.

198
00:15:00,314 --> 00:15:03,539
So I'm going to go to my wife in As-Sunh(ألصنح).

199
00:15:04,099 --> 00:15:06,220
At that time Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) had two wives,

200
00:15:06,391 --> 00:15:08,753
one wife in Madina and one wife in As-Sunh(ألصنح)

201
00:15:08,979 --> 00:15:11,145
which was on the outskirts of Madina.

202
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:15,768
So when he saw Rasool Allah ﷺ standing up and looking at them in Salah(صلاة)

203
00:15:16,159 --> 00:15:22,223
he felt that Rasool Ullah is getting better so I can go to As-Sunh(ألصنح) and that is her turn.

204
00:15:22,659 --> 00:15:25,631
Because he would spend one night here one night there. He said: This is her turn

205
00:15:26,239 --> 00:15:27,179
so he went to As-Sunh(ألصنح).

206
00:15:28,257 --> 00:15:34,091
But actually, Rasool Allah ﷺ was towards the last hours of his life.

207
00:15:36,328 --> 00:15:38,298
After Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the Sahabah(صحابه)

208
00:15:39,948 --> 00:15:44,307
and Allah comforted his heart in seeing the fruit of his Da'wah(دعوة).

209
00:15:47,192 --> 00:15:51,461
The burden of the illness was taking its toll on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

210
00:15:55,836 --> 00:16:03,914
Usama Bin Zayd(أسامه بن زيد) came in and Rasool Allah ﷺ was now unable to speak.

211
00:16:06,024 --> 00:16:08,973
Ayesha(عائشه) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ would raise his hand

212
00:16:09,152 --> 00:16:10,932
and then he would put it on Usama Bin Zayd(أسامه بن زيد)

213
00:16:11,388 --> 00:16:14,423
and then he would raise his hand and put it on Usama Bin Zayd(أسامه بن زيد).

214
00:16:15,006 --> 00:16:17,845
Ayesha(عائشه) said: We knew that Rasool Allah ﷺ was making Dua(دُعَا) for him.

215
00:16:19,301 --> 00:16:21,761
Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Usama Bin Zayd(أسامه بن زيد) so much, he said:

216
00:16:21,785 --> 00:16:22,723
ألحب إبن ألحب

217
00:16:22,957 --> 00:16:24,868
He is the Beloved, the son of the Beloved

218
00:16:25,205 --> 00:16:27,096
I loved his father and I loved him

219
00:16:27,425 --> 00:16:30,736
and Rasool Allah ﷺ actually adopted his father as his own son

220
00:16:31,002 --> 00:16:34,514
until adoption in that particular way was banned in Islam

221
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:37,339
where the person changes their name

222
00:16:37,859 --> 00:16:41,354
but Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Usama(أسامه) so much he was making Dua(دُعَا) for him.

223
00:16:42,239 --> 00:16:47,408
And then Ayesha(عائشه) said: So I held Rasool Allah ﷺ in my arms.

224
00:16:48,491 --> 00:16:50,338
وكان بين صحري ونحري

225
00:16:50,739 --> 00:16:56,895
So I was holding Rasool Allah ﷺ in my arms and he was between the bottom and the top of my chest

226
00:16:58,069 --> 00:17:01,278
 and I was holding him in my lap.

227
00:17:02,503 --> 00:17:05,679
And then my brother Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) came in and he had a Miswak(مسواك) with him.

228
00:17:06,803 --> 00:17:08,883
So Rasool Allah ﷺ was looking at the Miswak(مسواك)

229
00:17:08,904 --> 00:17:10,887
I realized that Rasool Allah ﷺ wants it.

230
00:17:11,875 --> 00:17:15,765
So I told him: Do you want it, Rasool Ullah nodded with his head yes.

231
00:17:16,943 --> 00:17:19,489
So Ayesha(عائشه) said: I took the Miswak(مسواك) from Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

232
00:17:19,724 --> 00:17:22,775
and I chewed it until I made it soft.

233
00:17:24,081 --> 00:17:26,852
And then I gave it to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he held it with his hand

234
00:17:27,176 --> 00:17:29,256
and he brushed his teeth, as if he was healthy.

235
00:17:30,268 --> 00:17:35,202
And all throughout, when he was using Miswak(مسواك), he was saying:

236
00:17:35,226 --> 00:17:38,178
بَلِ الرّفيقُ الأعْلَى، بَلِ الرّفيقُ الأعْلَى، بَلِ الرّفيقُ الأعْلَى

237
00:17:39,031 --> 00:17:41,996
The highest companion, the highest companion, the highest companion

238
00:17:43,452 --> 00:17:45,568
Rasool Allah ﷺ was speaking to who?

239
00:17:46,953 --> 00:17:48,425
He was speaking to the angel of death.

240
00:17:50,461 --> 00:17:52,072
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

241
00:17:52,406 --> 00:18:00,447
Every Nabi(نَبِي) before they die the Angel of Death comes and seeks permission from them to take their soul.

242
00:18:01,585 --> 00:18:06,499
See with you the angel of death will come unannounced and take it and leave.

243
00:18:06,924 --> 00:18:10,959
But with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah, out of respect for them.

244
00:18:11,328 --> 00:18:14,800
The Angel of Death asks them for permission first

245
00:18:15,542 --> 00:18:19,919
and that's when Musa(موسى) punched the angel of death in the well known story in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

246
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,601
Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying:

247
00:18:22,641 --> 00:18:23,671
بَلِ الرّفيقُ الأعْلَى

248
00:18:23,695 --> 00:18:26,048
The highest companion, the highest companion, the highest companion.

249
00:18:26,774 --> 00:18:30,277
Rasool Ullah was asking the question of the angel of death and saying I want to be with Allah,

250
00:18:30,372 --> 00:18:31,790
 the highest companion is Allah.

251
00:18:32,762 --> 00:18:37,866
I want to be with Allah, I'm ready to leave, I finished my mission.

252
00:18:39,862 --> 00:18:42,453
The Deen(دِيْن) is complete.

253
00:18:43,084 --> 00:18:48,535
اَلْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ وَأَتْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِي وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ الْإِسْلَامَ دِينًا

254
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:53,216
And then Ayesha رضي الله عنها said: Rasool Allah ﷺ would say

255
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:57,139
أللهم أغفرلي ورحمني ولحقني رفيق الأعلى

256
00:18:57,163 --> 00:19:00,200
O Allah forgive me and have mercy on me

257
00:19:00,846 --> 00:19:03,431
and make me join the highest companion, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

258
00:19:04,986 --> 00:19:08,087
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said and then Rasool Allah ﷺ raised up his hand

259
00:19:08,975 --> 00:19:09,779
and he would say;

260
00:19:09,803 --> 00:19:10,845
اللهم الرّفيقُ الأعْلَى

261
00:19:10,968 --> 00:19:14,596
The highest companion, the highest companion, the highest companion

262
00:19:14,941 --> 00:19:16,840
until she says his hand went down.

263
00:19:17,487 --> 00:19:19,364
And these were his last words

264
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,355
مَن أحَبَّ لقاءَ اللهِ أحَبَّ اللهُ لقاءَه

265
00:19:23,784 --> 00:19:26,690
The one, who loves to meet Allah, Allah would love to meet him.

266
00:19:27,354 --> 00:19:29,540
Rasool Allah ﷺ was eager to meet his Lord

267
00:19:30,074 --> 00:19:33,142
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ was eager to meet Muhammadﷺ.

268
00:19:35,394 --> 00:19:38,716
This is the greatest disaster that has occurred to the Ummah(امة).

269
00:19:40,122 --> 00:19:45,168
In the narration, it states, whenever one of you is afflicted with a calamity

270
00:19:45,192 --> 00:19:47,273
then remember your calamity in losing me

271
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,946
your calamity will become insignificant to you.

272
00:19:52,022 --> 00:19:55,723
If you ever go through trouble, if you ever go through a problem in your life

273
00:19:56,099 --> 00:20:01,137
remember that the biggest problem of all, the biggest disaster that happened to you

274
00:20:01,459 --> 00:20:03,124
is that Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

275
00:20:03,850 --> 00:20:08,837
If you remember that then your problem will be insignificant, it will become small.

276
00:20:11,484 --> 00:20:14,693
How did the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم deal with the situation?

277
00:20:16,617 --> 00:20:20,791
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, were very solid men, they were very strong.

278
00:20:21,341 --> 00:20:25,497
They were very capable of tackling any situation

279
00:20:26,756 --> 00:20:29,412
but the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ was something beyond.

280
00:20:30,375 --> 00:20:32,001
So Ibn Rajab Al-Hambali(إبن رجب الأحنبلي) says;

281
00:20:33,489 --> 00:20:37,215
ولم توفي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم من طرب المسلمون

282
00:20:37,539 --> 00:20:39,275
فمنهم من دوحش فخلد

283
00:20:40,045 --> 00:20:42,423
ومنهم من أقعد فلم يطقد قيام

284
00:20:42,615 --> 00:20:45,828
ومنهم من تقل لسانه فلم يطق الكلام

285
00:20:46,231 --> 00:20:48,496
ومنهم من انکر موته بالكله

286
00:20:49,398 --> 00:20:54,505
Ibn Rajab(إبن رجب) says: When Rasool Allah ﷺ died, a chaotic state ensued,

287
00:20:54,973 --> 00:20:58,247
 some of the Muslims, started to hallucinate

288
00:20:58,271 --> 00:21:00,148
and they didn't know what they were saying.

289
00:21:01,347 --> 00:21:04,761
While some of them sat down, and couldn't stand up.

290
00:21:05,671 --> 00:21:09,148
Some of them, their tongues would not move so they cannot speak

291
00:21:09,917 --> 00:21:12,697
and some of them refused to accept the fact that he died.

292
00:21:14,791 --> 00:21:18,696
And Al-Qazi Abu Bakr Ibn Arabi(ألقاضي ابوبكرإبن عربي) he states, he said;

293
00:21:19,057 --> 00:21:23,998
وطرف الحال فكان موت النبي قاسمة الزهري ومصيبت الأمر

294
00:21:25,166 --> 00:21:28,054
And a chaotic stage happened

295
00:21:28,691 --> 00:21:33,056
The death of Rasool Allah ﷺ was the event that broke their backs

296
00:21:33,381 --> 00:21:35,215
and was the disaster of their lives.

297
00:21:36,376 --> 00:21:39,120
أمَّا علي فستخفى بيت فاطمه

298
00:21:39,273 --> 00:21:41,677
Ali(علي) went into hiding in the house of Fatima(فاطمه)

299
00:21:42,485 --> 00:21:43,816
وامَّا عثمان  فسكت

300
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,505
And Uthman(عثمان) couldn't speak

301
00:21:46,017 --> 00:21:48,975
وأمَّا عمر فأهجر وقال ما مات رسول الله

302
00:21:49,221 --> 00:21:52,401
وإنَّما وعده ربه كما وعد موسى

303
00:21:52,585 --> 00:21:58,816
 وليرجعن رسول الله فاليقطعن ايدي رجالٍ وأرجلهم

304
00:21:59,446 --> 00:22:03,161
And Umar(عُمَر) went as far as claiming that Rasool Allah ﷺ did not die

305
00:22:03,509 --> 00:22:06,369
and he went to meet Allah for 40 days and he will come back

306
00:22:06,857 --> 00:22:10,877
and he will cut the feet and the arms of some people who claim that he died.

307
00:22:13,506 --> 00:22:16,772
So this was a very difficult time in their lives

308
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:19,949
and Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) says: I've seen two days in Madina.

309
00:22:21,094 --> 00:22:24,685
One day was the best day in Madina and that's when Rasool Allah ﷺ came.

310
00:22:25,244 --> 00:22:28,320
Everybody was happy, and Madina was full of light.

311
00:22:29,284 --> 00:22:32,623
And then I've witnessed and lived through the day when Rasool Allah ﷺ died

312
00:22:32,892 --> 00:22:34,248
and Madina became dark.

313
00:22:35,439 --> 00:22:38,803
The light was the light of Rasool Allah ﷺ and when he died the light went.

314
00:22:39,854 --> 00:22:41,788
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was at As-Sun'h(ألصنح).

315
00:22:42,675 --> 00:22:51,009
He received the news, so he came riding his horse straight to the room of Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

316
00:22:51,948 --> 00:22:54,569
And he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and uncovered his face

317
00:22:55,159 --> 00:22:58,102
and he kissed him on the forehead, and said: You are pure

318
00:22:58,598 --> 00:23:01,548
when you're alive, and you are pure, when you're dead.

319
00:23:02,498 --> 00:23:07,021
And he said: You have went through the death, which Allah has destined for you.

320
00:23:08,013 --> 00:23:09,198
And then he went to the Masjid(مسجد)

321
00:23:09,499 --> 00:23:11,942
while Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was speaking.

322
00:23:13,649 --> 00:23:16,790
And when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه started to talk

323
00:23:17,864 --> 00:23:20,324
Everyone left Umar(عُمَر) and they came to listen to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

324
00:23:22,344 --> 00:23:24,093
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

325
00:23:25,496 --> 00:23:29,141
من كان يعبد محمداً فإن محمداً قد مات

326
00:23:29,684 --> 00:23:32,520
ومن كان يعبد الله فإن الله حي لا يموت

327
00:23:33,977 --> 00:23:37,071
 وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلاَّ رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ

328
00:23:37,466 --> 00:23:40,452
 أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِكُمْ

329
00:23:40,661 --> 00:23:45,748
وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَى عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللهَ شَيْئًا وَسَيَجْزِي اللهُ الشَّاكِرِين۝

330
00:23:46,537 --> 00:23:53,351
A very brief speech, but it was a turning point in the history of this Ummah(امة), a few words.

331
00:23:54,298 --> 00:24:00,389
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: If you were worshipping Muhammad(محمد) then Muhammad(محمد) is dead.

332
00:24:01,309 --> 00:24:05,122
But if you're worshipping Allah than Allah is alive and He never dies.

333
00:24:06,119 --> 00:24:10,159
And then he recited the Ayah(آية), one, forty four(144) of Surat Al-Imram(سورة ألعمران)

334
00:24:11,270 --> 00:24:16,082
Muhammad(محمد) is not but a messenger, other messengers have passed on before him.

335
00:24:16,547 --> 00:24:22,010
So if he was to die, or to be killed, would you turn back on your heels to unbelief.

336
00:24:22,874 --> 00:24:26,600
And he who turns back on his heels will never harm Allah at all.

337
00:24:26,964 --> 00:24:28,600
But Allah will reward the grateful.

338
00:24:30,136 --> 00:24:34,015
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: When I heard that Ayah(آية)

339
00:24:34,753 --> 00:24:36,314
from the mouth of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

340
00:24:36,646 --> 00:24:39,186
It was as if it was the first time I ever hear the Ayah(آية).

341
00:24:39,636 --> 00:24:41,916
Even though Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was a Hafiz(حافظ) of Qur'an.

342
00:24:43,216 --> 00:24:46,703
But he didn't imagine that the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ would happen at that moment.

343
00:24:46,727 --> 00:24:48,624
Now this Ayah(آية) was revealed in the Ghazwa(غزوة) of Uhud(أحَد)

344
00:24:48,649 --> 00:24:51,678
 when there was a rumor that Rasool Allah ﷺ was killed in the battle.

345
00:24:52,003 --> 00:24:55,280
So some of the Sahabah(صحابه) sat down when they heard that rumor in Uhud(أحَد) and said;

346
00:24:55,526 --> 00:24:59,455
 We're not gonna fight, why should we fight when Muhammadﷺ was killed, we should just stay here.

347
00:25:00,136 --> 00:25:04,219
So Allah is telling them, and if Muhammadﷺ is killed or he dies

348
00:25:04,372 --> 00:25:09,166
you would go back to unbelief, even if he dies, you have to carry on with your message

349
00:25:09,467 --> 00:25:12,063
and fight on what Muhammadﷺ was fighting on.

350
00:25:13,723 --> 00:25:17,707
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: When I heard Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) recite that Ayah(آية)

351
00:25:18,385 --> 00:25:23,993
my feet failed, my legs fails to carry me so I fell down on my knees

352
00:25:24,435 --> 00:25:26,918
and I realized that Muhammadﷺ was dead.

353
00:25:27,688 --> 00:25:30,632
Imagine Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the strong powerful man

354
00:25:30,917 --> 00:25:35,550
his feet wouldn't carry him anymore so he falls down, on his knees.

355
00:25:37,617 --> 00:25:41,334
The narrator says, and then you could only hear crying in the Masjid(مسجد).

356
00:25:42,103 --> 00:25:46,447
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, was the one, who brought them back to reality.

357
00:25:48,052 --> 00:25:52,510
And Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says: This is an evidence that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) has the strongest heart,

358
00:25:52,971 --> 00:25:54,861
 because who was the one closest to Muhammadﷺ?

359
00:25:54,990 --> 00:25:55,795
it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

360
00:25:56,041 --> 00:26:00,057
So if there was going to be anyone who should have failed in this situation,

361
00:26:00,406 --> 00:26:03,186
 because of the weight of it, it would have been Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

362
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:07,178
 because he was the one, who loved Rasool Allah ﷺ

363
00:26:07,292 --> 00:26:10,600
and has been associated with him more than anybody else.

364
00:26:10,868 --> 00:26:16,201
Nevertheless, he was the one, who brought them back and unified the Sahabah(صحابه)

365
00:26:17,049 --> 00:26:20,888
and made them realize that yes, this was the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah and it happened.

366
00:26:22,406 --> 00:26:26,607
And this is one of the standing moments in the life of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

367
00:26:26,712 --> 00:26:30,139
a very short speech, but it was a turning point, for the Ummah(امة).

368
00:26:32,088 --> 00:26:34,650
Later on that day, Monday, same day, the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم

369
00:26:36,091 --> 00:26:42,449
the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم, started gathering in Saqeefat Banni Sa'adah(ثقيقة بني سعدة)

370
00:26:43,493 --> 00:26:48,754
a shed, belonging to Bannu Sa'ada(بنوسعدة), a meeting place.

371
00:26:50,459 --> 00:26:52,490
In the beginning it was Al-Aos and Al-Khazraj(ألأوس والخزرج)

372
00:26:52,514 --> 00:26:54,734
and then Al-Aos(ألأوس) left and it was only Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

373
00:26:55,308 --> 00:26:56,729
What were they discussing?

374
00:26:57,182 --> 00:26:59,265
They were discussing appointing an Ameer(أمير).

375
00:27:01,638 --> 00:27:09,002
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was busy with the burial proceedings of Rasool Allah ﷺ when somebody came and called him.

376
00:27:09,391 --> 00:27:10,614
Umar(عُمَر) said: I'm busy.

377
00:27:11,266 --> 00:27:15,217
The man said: Come out because something important has happened

378
00:27:15,448 --> 00:27:20,305
Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) have gathered in the portico in the Saqeefah(ثقيفه) of Bannu Sa'adah(بنوسعدة).

379
00:27:21,948 --> 00:27:23,470
And war could breakout.

380
00:27:24,486 --> 00:27:29,838
Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) were two tribes Al-Aos Wal-Khazraj(ألأوس والخزرج) they fought each other for ages

381
00:27:29,925 --> 00:27:32,368
and it was Rasool Allah ﷺ who brought them together.

382
00:27:34,176 --> 00:27:37,259
And Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) can come in any moment and cause Fitnah(فِتْنَه) between people.

383
00:27:39,638 --> 00:27:42,863
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went out, and this is in one narration.

384
00:27:43,728 --> 00:27:44,870
In the narration of Bukhari(بخاريْ),

385
00:27:44,918 --> 00:27:51,453
it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) who went to Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) in Saqeefat Banni Sa'adah(ثقيقة بني سعدة).

386
00:27:52,568 --> 00:27:55,982
When they were going there they met with two men from Al-Aos(ألأوس).

387
00:27:56,730 --> 00:27:58,259
They told them: Where are you going?

388
00:27:58,981 --> 00:28:02,645
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) said: We're going to the meeting place of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

389
00:28:04,102 --> 00:28:06,913
They said: Don't worry about it.

390
00:28:07,222 --> 00:28:10,048
You go ahead and make your decision, Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون)

391
00:28:10,452 --> 00:28:12,152
- go ahead and make your decision.

392
00:28:13,242 --> 00:28:16,938
And don't worry about Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار), and their gathering.

393
00:28:17,425 --> 00:28:19,490
Meaning this affair belongs to Al-Muhajireen(مهاجرين)

394
00:28:19,899 --> 00:28:21,349
you go ahead and make the decision

395
00:28:21,389 --> 00:28:24,441
you don't have to go and meet with Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) at this moment.

396
00:28:24,665 --> 00:28:27,977
Umar(عُمَر) said: No! We will go to them, because it is Shura(شورى)

397
00:28:29,183 --> 00:28:31,026
we're not going to make our decision on our own.

398
00:28:31,233 --> 00:28:36,849
We're gonna, it's going to be through Shura(شورى), so they went in to Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

399
00:28:37,518 --> 00:28:41,790
There was somebody sitting among them who was covered, in a blanket.

400
00:28:42,231 --> 00:28:43,397
So Umar(عُمَر) said: Who's that?

401
00:28:43,492 --> 00:28:46,758
They said: This is Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدإبن عبادة), and he is ill

402
00:28:46,956 --> 00:28:48,520
he had a fever and he was very ill.

403
00:28:49,899 --> 00:28:52,165
Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدإبن عبادة) was the leader of Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج)

404
00:28:52,998 --> 00:28:57,046
And he was the one, they wanted to appoint as Ameer(أمير).

405
00:28:58,831 --> 00:29:02,463
Sa'ad Ibn Ubadah(سعدإبن عبادة) was a very well known figure among Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار)

406
00:29:02,487 --> 00:29:04,473
and Rasool Allah ﷺ loved him very much.

407
00:29:06,274 --> 00:29:09,577
And they wanted to appoint him as a leader for the Muslim community.

408
00:29:09,926 --> 00:29:13,363
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: We went in and we sat down.

409
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:16,958
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: And I was preparing a speech

410
00:29:18,191 --> 00:29:20,744
I was bringing together a speech to present.

411
00:29:22,904 --> 00:29:25,503
So he was preparing, what to say.

412
00:29:27,047 --> 00:29:30,930
He said: And then the Speaker of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) stood up.

413
00:29:31,339 --> 00:29:34,617
This was a formal meeting so one speaker from Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) would stand

414
00:29:35,338 --> 00:29:37,902
and he praise Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that's how they would start

415
00:29:38,102 --> 00:29:42,278
their Khut'ba(خطبة), their talk by the Al-Hamdulillah(ألحمدلله), praising Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

416
00:29:42,309 --> 00:29:44,189
and making Salah(صلاة) on Muhammadﷺ.

417
00:29:46,146 --> 00:29:46,939
And then he said;

418
00:29:47,990 --> 00:29:48,835
نحن الأنصار

419
00:29:49,097 --> 00:29:52,885
We the Ansaar(أنْصَار), are the helpers of Allah

420
00:29:53,268 --> 00:29:55,820
Ansaar(أنْصَار), that's the meaning of Ansaar(أنْصَار), the helpers.

421
00:29:56,464 --> 00:29:57,662
وكَتِيْبَةُ الْإسلام

422
00:29:57,730 --> 00:30:01,693
And we are the battalion of Islam, we are the army of this religion

423
00:30:02,359 --> 00:30:08,388
while Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) are a few immigrants, small in number who left their people.

424
00:30:08,981 --> 00:30:12,863
But now they want to strip away from us, this authority.

425
00:30:14,911 --> 00:30:17,424
In other words, this man was saying

426
00:30:17,990 --> 00:30:23,722
that the leadership of the community should now transfer to the Ansaar(أنْصَار) after Rasool Allah ﷺ.

427
00:30:24,278 --> 00:30:28,341
And he says that, Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) are the army of Islam while Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) are few in number

428
00:30:28,381 --> 00:30:32,589
 and that's true Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) were much few in terms of numbers

429
00:30:32,669 --> 00:30:36,956
they were way less compared to Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنه

430
00:30:37,297 --> 00:30:42,148
in every battle, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) would be the majority the Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) are the minority

431
00:30:42,768 --> 00:30:44,468
and this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

432
00:30:48,327 --> 00:30:51,090
In other words he's saying that we should give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعدبن عبادة).

433
00:30:52,477 --> 00:30:56,200
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) stood up to speak

434
00:30:57,072 --> 00:30:58,862
because he has already prepared the speech.

435
00:30:59,420 --> 00:31:04,903
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: Umar(عُمَر), take it easy and sit down,

436
00:31:05,538 --> 00:31:09,532
until I deliver my speech and complete it and then say whatever you want.

437
00:31:10,475 --> 00:31:11,374
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

438
00:31:11,398 --> 00:31:13,025
وكنت أداري منه بعد الحد

439
00:31:13,049 --> 00:31:17,327
And because of the temper of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) I didn't want to anger him so I sat down.

440
00:31:19,917 --> 00:31:23,788
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه stood up and he started to speak.

441
00:31:25,035 --> 00:31:26,310
Among the things he said,

442
00:31:27,977 --> 00:31:30,112
maybe not all of this speech has survived

443
00:31:30,190 --> 00:31:33,432
because there's bits and pieces in different narrations, he said;

444
00:31:34,304 --> 00:31:38,010
And what you have mentioned about yourself, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) is undeniable

445
00:31:38,131 --> 00:31:38,877
 that's the truth.

446
00:31:40,045 --> 00:31:43,040
When you say that you are the army of Islam, that's the truth.

447
00:31:43,693 --> 00:31:46,042
When you are the helpers of Allah, that's the truth.

448
00:31:46,460 --> 00:31:49,249
And he added to that by narrating the Ayaat(آيات)

449
00:31:49,274 --> 00:31:51,875
and the Ahadith(احاديث) that were praising Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

450
00:31:53,372 --> 00:31:55,242
And he said that Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

451
00:31:55,708 --> 00:31:58,841
If the Ansaar(أنْصَار) would take one way,

452
00:31:59,432 --> 00:32:02,010
while all of the other people take another way

453
00:32:02,210 --> 00:32:03,964
I will follow the way of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

454
00:32:06,273 --> 00:32:08,610
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said that I am with you

455
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:12,261
my life and my death will be among Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

456
00:32:12,867 --> 00:32:15,751
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah, he refused to go back to Makkah

457
00:32:15,775 --> 00:32:17,640
and he went back with Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) to Madina.

458
00:32:18,652 --> 00:32:23,490
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) brought up all of these Ahadith(احاديث), praising Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

459
00:32:23,955 --> 00:32:31,836
But then he said: But the Arabs will never approve leadership in the hands of anyone but the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

460
00:32:34,485 --> 00:32:39,297
The Arabs were divided tribes and every tribe had his own pride.

461
00:32:40,614 --> 00:32:42,588
And it's very difficult to bring them together

462
00:32:43,014 --> 00:32:45,999
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is saying that the only people

463
00:32:46,683 --> 00:32:50,534
whom the Arabs would be willing to submit to, are the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

464
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:54,301
Because Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), it has been established in their hearts

465
00:32:54,821 --> 00:32:58,157
that they are the nobility of Arabia and they are the protectors of Al-Haram(ألحرم).

466
00:32:58,864 --> 00:33:05,000
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), he held up the hands of Umar(عُمَر) and Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) and he said;

467
00:33:05,736 --> 00:33:11,864
And I would be satisfied with either one of these two men being our Ameer(أمير)

468
00:33:12,478 --> 00:33:14,659
so give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to whichever one you want.

469
00:33:15,683 --> 00:33:16,778
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

470
00:33:17,282 --> 00:33:20,693
Everything that I wanted to say in my prepared speech

471
00:33:21,525 --> 00:33:25,333
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) has said it, and better in his impromptu speech.

472
00:33:26,369 --> 00:33:29,667
He said: I was preparing this speech and thinking about it

473
00:33:29,749 --> 00:33:31,898
all throughout the way until I got there.

474
00:33:33,346 --> 00:33:37,068
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) he said it, in a better way and a more complete way

475
00:33:37,101 --> 00:33:42,110
and he added to add things that I have missed in an impromptu speech.

476
00:33:43,216 --> 00:33:46,038
He said: The only thing that I didn't like was his last statement

477
00:33:46,454 --> 00:33:47,974
asking to give a Baiyah(بَيْعة) to me.

478
00:33:49,017 --> 00:33:50,472
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said and

479
00:33:50,503 --> 00:33:52,231
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) look at the statement, he said;

480
00:33:53,540 --> 00:33:59,152
In the Name of Allah, I would rather be taken ahead and beheaded

481
00:34:00,317 --> 00:34:03,785
then become an Ameer(أمير), over people and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is one of them.

482
00:34:04,562 --> 00:34:06,820
I would never want to be a leader of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

483
00:34:06,844 --> 00:34:11,743
I would rather die than assume leadership over Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

484
00:34:12,310 --> 00:34:14,246
He saw it as inappropriate.

485
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:19,339
How could I be in the position of leadership and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is behind me.?

486
00:34:19,990 --> 00:34:22,189
He said: I would rather die, they cut my neck.

487
00:34:23,464 --> 00:34:25,834
Al-Khabbab Bin Mundhir(ألخباب بن منذر) stood up and said;

488
00:34:26,432 --> 00:34:29,328
I have a solution, he is one of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

489
00:34:29,517 --> 00:34:34,990
How about a Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) appoint an Ameer(أمير) and we appoint an Ameer(أمير).

490
00:34:36,284 --> 00:34:39,997
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You cannot have two swords in one sheath

491
00:34:40,541 --> 00:34:44,787
two swords can't go together, it has to be one leader.

492
00:34:45,738 --> 00:34:47,499
And then there was an argument that happened

493
00:34:47,523 --> 00:34:51,382
and the voices were being raised.

494
00:34:52,761 --> 00:34:54,957
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I feared Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

495
00:34:55,828 --> 00:34:57,639
So I went ahead and told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

496
00:34:57,953 --> 00:35:01,229
Extend your hand forward so I will give you Baiyah(بَيْعة).

497
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:04,954
And then I gave my Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

498
00:35:05,155 --> 00:35:07,069
And then the Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) followed

499
00:35:07,300 --> 00:35:09,426
and then the Ansaar(أنْصَار) came and gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة)

500
00:35:09,952 --> 00:35:13,039
and they were doing it with such emotions

501
00:35:13,245 --> 00:35:18,269
because they came to realize that yes, how could we appoint an Ameer(أمير), and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is around.

502
00:35:19,766 --> 00:35:21,439
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) later on, said:

503
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:27,916
يا معشرالأنصار ألستم تعلمون أنَّ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم امارة ابوبكرأن يا أمة با الناس

504
00:35:28,211 --> 00:35:30,959
فايكم تطيب نفسه ان يتقدم ابا بكر

505
00:35:31,735 --> 00:35:33,360
He said: O people of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار)

506
00:35:33,704 --> 00:35:37,635
Don't you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ has appointed Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be our Imam(اِمَام)

507
00:35:38,338 --> 00:35:41,286
who of you can stand ahead and be an Imam(اِمَام)

508
00:35:41,689 --> 00:35:42,777
while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is Ma'moor(معمور).

509
00:35:44,683 --> 00:35:47,099
Rasool Allah ﷺ has appointed him to be our Imam(اِمَام) in Salah(صلاة)

510
00:35:47,124 --> 00:35:49,771
and the Khalifah(خليفه) will be the one, who will be Imam(اِمَام) of Salah(صلاة).

511
00:35:50,134 --> 00:35:52,779
Can any one of you lead Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in Salah(صلاة). They said:

512
00:35:52,819 --> 00:35:53,459
نعوذوبالله

513
00:35:53,531 --> 00:35:54,593
We seek refuge in Allah.

514
00:35:55,790 --> 00:36:00,319
So they came back to realize that it is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who should be the Khalifah(خليفه)

515
00:36:00,437 --> 00:36:03,020
so they all jumped on Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to give him Baiyah(بَيْعة)

516
00:36:03,243 --> 00:36:06,455
and they were stepping over Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد إبن عبادة), who was ill.

517
00:36:07,709 --> 00:36:10,527
And they were saying be careful, you're going to kill Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعد إبن عبادة)

518
00:36:11,563 --> 00:36:14,651
 so this wasn't nationalism or tribalism.

519
00:36:15,287 --> 00:36:18,171
They were searching for the truth and whenever they would find it

520
00:36:18,548 --> 00:36:19,599
they would hold on to it.

521
00:36:21,173 --> 00:36:26,659
A few notes on the affair of the Saqeefat Bannu Sa'adah(ثقيفة بنوسعدة).

522
00:36:26,683 --> 00:36:32,842
First of all, both Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) Umar  رضي الله عنهما were not seeking leadership.

523
00:36:33,914 --> 00:36:35,705
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as we have mentioned he said:

524
00:36:35,729 --> 00:36:39,270
I would rather be beheaded, rather than assume leadership over Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

525
00:36:39,711 --> 00:36:43,831
while Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said, in a Khut'ba(خطبة). He said:

526
00:36:43,855 --> 00:36:47,800
والله ما كنت حريصًا على العِمارة يومًا ولا ليلةً قط

527
00:36:48,273 --> 00:36:53,051
He said: I've never been eager to become an Ameer(أمير), in any night or in any day

528
00:36:54,166 --> 00:36:55,716
ولا كنت فيها راغبًا

529
00:36:56,368 --> 00:36:59,393
And I have never wanted it to come to me

530
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:03,419
ولا سعلته الله عزَّوَجل في سرٍّ وعلانية

531
00:37:03,775 --> 00:37:07,618
And I have never prayed to Allah to make me an Ameer(أمير) in public or in private

532
00:37:09,395 --> 00:37:11,534
ولكني أشفقتم من الفتنة

533
00:37:12,031 --> 00:37:14,181
But I was afraid that it would become a Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

534
00:37:14,630 --> 00:37:17,560
I was afraid of disunity among the Ummah(امة) and that's why I accepted it

535
00:37:18,017 --> 00:37:19,655
I accepted it for the benefit of the Ummah(امة).

536
00:37:20,589 --> 00:37:22,099
ومالي في إمارة في المراء

537
00:37:22,123 --> 00:37:26,731
And I'm having no rest, I'm having no peace of mind in this position of leadership.

538
00:37:27,368 --> 00:37:30,797
ولكن قلت أمرًا عظيمًا مالي بهم من طاقة،

539
00:37:31,034 --> 00:37:36,965
ولا يده إلَّا بتقوية الله عزوجل ولا ودت أنَّ أقو الناس عليها ماكان

540
00:37:37,049 --> 00:37:43,232
And he said: I have no ability to bear this responsibility, unless Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gives me strength

541
00:37:43,589 --> 00:37:47,367
and I am desiring that somebody is stronger than me, would take it from me.

542
00:37:48,521 --> 00:37:53,582
They didn't want to become leaders, they weren't seeking Imarah(إمارة)

543
00:37:54,313 --> 00:37:58,240
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) says that the reason I accepted it, is to keep the Ummah(امة) away from Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

544
00:38:01,156 --> 00:38:03,136
When Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said that

545
00:38:04,624 --> 00:38:08,046
people would not submit, except to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

546
00:38:08,793 --> 00:38:13,900
There are actually a Hadith(حديث) in that narrated by 40 Among the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

547
00:38:14,857 --> 00:38:20,069
 many narrations one of them, that the leadership is in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

548
00:38:21,182 --> 00:38:22,755
إنَّ هذالأمر في قريش

549
00:38:22,913 --> 00:38:26,514
This affair is in the hands of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

550
00:38:27,485 --> 00:38:29,277
That is because of their status.

551
00:38:30,046 --> 00:38:34,427
 So Rasool Allah ﷺ said that the position of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) and this is only Khilafah(خِلَافَه)

552
00:38:34,451 --> 00:38:36,427
it's not talking about other positions of leadership.

553
00:38:36,824 --> 00:38:39,878
It is strictly speaking about the position of Khalifah(خليفه)

554
00:38:40,226 --> 00:38:44,434
the highest position, Khifat(خلافت) Rasool Allah ﷺ.

555
00:38:46,993 --> 00:38:53,743
The Ahadith(احاديث) that indicated the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

556
00:38:54,676 --> 00:38:58,782
There are many indications and hints to the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

557
00:38:59,310 --> 00:39:03,845
Number one: This Hadith(حديث) is in, Muslim(مسلم)

558
00:39:05,169 --> 00:39:11,374
أَتَتِ امْرَأَةٌ النبيَّ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ، فأمَرَهَا أنْ تَرْجِعَ إلَيْهِ

559
00:39:12,542 --> 00:39:17,408
قَالَتْ: أرَأَيْتَ إنْ جِئْتُ ولَمْ أجِدْكَ؟ كَأنَّهَا تَقُولُ: المَوْتَ

560
00:39:18,349 --> 00:39:21,680
قَالَ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ: إنْ لَمْ تَجِدِينِي فَأْتي أبَا بَكْرٍ

561
00:39:22,856 --> 00:39:24,684
A women came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

562
00:39:25,501 --> 00:39:28,941
Rasool Allah ﷺ made an appointment with her and told her to come back

563
00:39:29,843 --> 00:39:32,397
it's either a question or a certain thing that she needed.

564
00:39:33,409 --> 00:39:36,627
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her, come back and he made an appointment with her.

565
00:39:37,334 --> 00:39:40,044
She said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I didn't find you.

566
00:39:41,243 --> 00:39:44,976
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If you don't find me, then go to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

567
00:39:47,168 --> 00:39:49,174
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني), he says;

568
00:39:49,600 --> 00:39:56,655
وفي الحديث أنَّا مواعيد النبي كانت على من يتول الخلافة بعده تنجيزها

569
00:39:57,097 --> 00:40:02,601
وفيه ردٌّ على شيعة في زعمِهم أنَّه نسَّها إستخلاف علي والعبَّاس

570
00:40:02,625 --> 00:40:04,311
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني), says:

571
00:40:04,922 --> 00:40:13,645
In this Hadith(حديث) is an evidence that the appointments of Rasool Allah ﷺ are to be carried on by the Khalifah(خليفه) after him.

572
00:40:14,452 --> 00:40:18,841
And the Khalifah(خليفه) after him is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and here is a response to Shia(شيعة),

573
00:40:18,881 --> 00:40:22,660
 who claim that the Khalifah(خليفه) should have Ali(علي) or Al-Abbas(العباس).

574
00:40:23,570 --> 00:40:27,710
This is a very interesting point made by Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني).

575
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:32,811
He says that this is a clear indication that Rasool Allah ﷺ considers his deputy

576
00:40:33,808 --> 00:40:36,663
the one to take responsibility in his absence is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

577
00:40:37,871 --> 00:40:42,548
Rasool Allah ﷺ has already made it clear that the Imam(اِمَام) in Salah(صلاة) is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

578
00:40:42,588 --> 00:40:44,295
and Salah(صلاة) is؛ the religion.

579
00:40:45,048 --> 00:40:48,673
Now this woman came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, maybe for a Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) issue.

580
00:40:49,138 --> 00:40:51,755
Either she wants Sadaqah(صدقة) or she has a question or...

581
00:40:52,501 --> 00:40:55,698
And Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling her, if you don't find me then go to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

582
00:40:55,723 --> 00:40:58,052
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the leader in the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) affairs

583
00:40:58,076 --> 00:41:00,410
and in the religious affairs, in both.

584
00:41:01,563 --> 00:41:02,992
And in Islam they were combined

585
00:41:03,017 --> 00:41:05,498
so the Imam(اِمَام) of the Salah(صلاة) is the leader of the community.

586
00:41:07,159 --> 00:41:11,122
So it's very clear evidence that Rasool Allah ﷺ was actually saying

587
00:41:11,314 --> 00:41:14,788
the one who should assume the responsibility after me, is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

588
00:41:15,175 --> 00:41:17,634
If you don't find me, then go to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

589
00:41:19,138 --> 00:41:24,634
Number two, Hudaifah رضي الله عنه said, and this Hadith(حديث) is in Tirimdi(ترمذي).

590
00:41:25,959 --> 00:41:29,151
He said: We were sitting with Rasool Allah ﷺ in a gathering.

591
00:41:29,452 --> 00:41:34,311
So he said: I don't know how long I will last among you

592
00:41:35,744 --> 00:41:38,778
but follow the two, who will come after me

593
00:41:39,524 --> 00:41:41,733
and he pointed Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

594
00:41:42,693 --> 00:41:47,467
And he said: And hold on to the covenant of Ammar(عَمَّار).

595
00:41:47,979 --> 00:41:52,838
And whatever Ibn Masood(إبن مسعود) narrates of my Hadith(حديث), then believe in it.

596
00:41:53,869 --> 00:41:56,311
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ was pointing to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر)

597
00:41:56,336 --> 00:42:00,159
and say follow their way, meaning these are the leaders after me.

598
00:42:01,303 --> 00:42:06,773
Number three, Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه narrates and this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(مسلم).

599
00:42:07,683 --> 00:42:09,325
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream,

600
00:42:10,103 --> 00:42:14,264
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that he was sitting next to a pool,

601
00:42:15,216 --> 00:42:18,887
and he was drawing water for the people to drink.

602
00:42:19,177 --> 00:42:22,252
In the old days, you'd have a pool next to the well.

603
00:42:22,593 --> 00:42:25,677
So you'd draw water out of the well and you would pour it in the pool

604
00:42:25,884 --> 00:42:27,894
so people would drink directly from the pool.

605
00:42:29,538 --> 00:42:32,817
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I was drawing out water from the well

606
00:42:33,345 --> 00:42:34,901
and pouring it into my pool.

607
00:42:35,335 --> 00:42:38,460
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted me to rest

608
00:42:38,882 --> 00:42:41,967
so he held the bucket, and he started pulling out water

609
00:42:42,541 --> 00:42:43,869
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

610
00:42:44,240 --> 00:42:46,708
وفي نضعه ضعف ولله يغفروله

611
00:42:47,244 --> 00:42:49,996
And his pulling was weak, my Allah forgive him.

612
00:42:51,508 --> 00:42:52,871
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

613
00:42:52,895 --> 00:42:56,883
And then Umar(عُمَر) came and he took the bucket from Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

614
00:42:57,332 --> 00:43:02,746
So Rasool Allah ﷺ says: I have never seen a man stronger in drawing out the water like Umar(عُمَر)

615
00:43:03,390 --> 00:43:06,865
and when he left the pool was flowing with water and it was splashing.

616
00:43:08,650 --> 00:43:12,766
Ash-Shafie(ألشافعي) gives an interpretation to this dream. He says;

617
00:43:13,466 --> 00:43:14,821
رؤیاء الأنبياء وحي

618
00:43:15,396 --> 00:43:18,518
The dreams of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), are a form of Revelation.

619
00:43:19,324 --> 00:43:23,959
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said: And there was weakness in the drawing of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

620
00:43:23,999 --> 00:43:30,061
 It means that his time in Khilafah(خِلَافَه) will be very short, it won't be long.

621
00:43:31,092 --> 00:43:33,616
And that he will be busy with the Harb(حرب) of Riddah(ردة).

622
00:43:34,128 --> 00:43:36,089
So he's not going to make a lot of opening,

623
00:43:36,546 --> 00:43:38,610
so he's not going to spread the water all over.

624
00:43:38,848 --> 00:43:41,311
See, the water from the well is the religion of Islam.

625
00:43:41,893 --> 00:43:44,140
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) his Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was very short.

626
00:43:44,643 --> 00:43:48,319
And he didn't have a chance to spread out the religion very far

627
00:43:48,344 --> 00:43:50,683
because he only became a Khalifah(خليفه) for a little over two years.

628
00:43:51,796 --> 00:43:53,710
And then Ash-Shafie(ألشافعي) says;

629
00:43:54,144 --> 00:43:55,811
الذي بلغ وعمرفي طول مدت

630
00:43:56,144 --> 00:43:58,789
His Khalifah(خليفه) wasn't as long as Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar(عُمَر)

631
00:43:59,043 --> 00:44:02,834
and Umar(عُمَر) devoted his time in Khilafah(خِلَافَه) to spreading out the message.

632
00:44:04,292 --> 00:44:07,585
Jihad(جهاد) against the enemies of Allah and spreading the Deen(دِيْن) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

633
00:44:08,276 --> 00:44:11,385
and that's how the water filled the pool and it was splashing out.

634
00:44:13,061 --> 00:44:17,093
So it's considered that this Hadith(حديث) is also an indication that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the next Khalifah(خليفه),

635
00:44:17,133 --> 00:44:19,745
and he will be followed by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

636
00:44:23,449 --> 00:44:25,999
Number four, and this is a Muslim(مسلم) too.

637
00:44:26,245 --> 00:44:28,094
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said;

638
00:44:28,581 --> 00:44:30,993
Rasool Allah ﷺ told me, when he was ill.

639
00:44:31,236 --> 00:44:35,772
Call your father Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and call your brother Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن),

640
00:44:36,213 --> 00:44:40,602
 so that I can write a covenant, a will.

641
00:44:41,595 --> 00:44:45,857
 Because I'm afraid that somebody might desire this

642
00:44:46,416 --> 00:44:50,943
and say that it is more appropriate for me to be in this position.

643
00:44:51,502 --> 00:44:54,882
But Allah, and the believers, only want Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

644
00:44:56,269 --> 00:44:58,937
Allah and the believers only want Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

645
00:44:59,324 --> 00:45:04,640
Rasool Ullah was saying hand me a paper so that I will write down a document

646
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:06,788
 stating that the Khalifah(خليفه) after me is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

647
00:45:07,628 --> 00:45:10,739
because I'm afraid that somebody might come and try to claim it

648
00:45:11,587 --> 00:45:13,818
and say that it belongs to me.

649
00:45:14,384 --> 00:45:17,370
When Allah and the believers want Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

650
00:45:18,015 --> 00:45:19,200
Now that did not happened.

651
00:45:19,518 --> 00:45:21,628
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not write the covenant.

652
00:45:22,169 --> 00:45:26,597
And we'll talk about that later on, on the implications of that.

653
00:45:27,719 --> 00:45:32,754
Number five, the Hadith(حديث) of Salah(صلاة), which she mentioned briefly.

654
00:45:34,189 --> 00:45:35,530
And this is in Muslim(مسلم).

655
00:45:36,411 --> 00:45:38,313
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was ill.

656
00:45:39,029 --> 00:45:41,232
He asked: Did the people pray? They said: No.

657
00:45:41,745 --> 00:45:45,081
They're waiting for you, so he said: Put some water for me.

658
00:45:45,246 --> 00:45:49,948
So Rasool Allah ﷺ went and they would pour this water on his body to cool it down.

659
00:45:50,656 --> 00:45:55,491
His temperature were very was very high so he would pour a cold water on his body

660
00:45:55,768 --> 00:45:57,154
but then he fell unconscious.

661
00:45:58,109 --> 00:46:00,349
And when he woke up, he said: Did they pray? They said: No!

662
00:46:00,373 --> 00:46:05,369
They're waiting for you, he said: Bring me water and he was trying to prepare himself for Salah(صلاة)

663
00:46:05,409 --> 00:46:07,134
 but every time, he would fall unconscious,

664
00:46:07,663 --> 00:46:09,555
and that happened three times and then he said;

665
00:46:09,623 --> 00:46:11,411
Tell Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the people in Salah(صلاة).

666
00:46:12,187 --> 00:46:14,291
When they told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the people in Salah(صلاة)

667
00:46:14,371 --> 00:46:16,777
He told Umar(عُمَر), Why don't you lead them to Salah(صلاة)?

668
00:46:16,931 --> 00:46:18,343
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No.

669
00:46:18,367 --> 00:46:20,529
You should be the one, who was leading the Salah(صلاة)

670
00:46:21,948 --> 00:46:26,593
So here's another indication that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) considered

671
00:46:27,046 --> 00:46:29,297
Umar(عُمَر) to be the second in command after him.

672
00:46:30,463 --> 00:46:33,075
And that's why he told him to go and lead but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: No.

673
00:46:33,425 --> 00:46:35,854
You are the one, who should be the Imam(اِمَام).

674
00:46:36,697 --> 00:46:41,754
So this is other evidence that the Imam(اِمَام) of the Salah(صلاة) is the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims

675
00:46:42,113 --> 00:46:44,356
and Rasool Allah ﷺ clearly said that it is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

676
00:46:44,782 --> 00:46:45,923
Number six,

677
00:46:49,489 --> 00:46:52,311
The conversation that happened in the Saqeefah(ثقيفه) the Ansaar(أنْصَار) said;

678
00:46:52,613 --> 00:46:54,904
 One Ameer(أمير) from us and one Ameer(أمير) from you.

679
00:46:55,292 --> 00:46:58,882
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told them. O, people of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار):

680
00:46:59,418 --> 00:47:03,461
Don't you remember that Rasool Allah ﷺ has actually told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the people in Salah(صلاة).

681
00:47:03,786 --> 00:47:07,619
Who of you would like to be the Imam(اِمَام) while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is praying behind them.

682
00:47:08,213 --> 00:47:08,763
 And they said;

683
00:47:08,803 --> 00:47:09,433
نعوذوبالله

684
00:47:09,473 --> 00:47:10,488
We seek refuge in Allah.

685
00:47:11,555 --> 00:47:14,472
We would never want to be ahead of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

686
00:47:15,695 --> 00:47:16,528
Number seven,

687
00:47:18,392 --> 00:47:21,432
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), he narrates, he says;

688
00:47:22,421 --> 00:47:24,513
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

689
00:47:25,798 --> 00:47:30,430
And we found that he has actually appointed Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be the Imam(اِمَام) in the Salah(صلاة).

690
00:47:31,251 --> 00:47:36,767
We said: If Rasool Allah ﷺ was pleased to have Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) lead us in our religion,

691
00:47:37,940 --> 00:47:40,728
then he should also be our leader in the worldly affairs.

692
00:47:41,365 --> 00:47:43,586
Because the religious affairs are higher in status

693
00:47:44,067 --> 00:47:47,020
and since Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was appointed to lead us in religion

694
00:47:47,696 --> 00:47:51,820
then it only makes sense that he would also be the one to lead us in our worldly affairs.

695
00:47:52,098 --> 00:47:55,644
And this is a statement by, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

696
00:47:55,929 --> 00:47:57,364
in Tabaqaat Ibn Sa'ad(طبقات إبن سعد).

697
00:48:01,290 --> 00:48:07,720
Ahlus-Sunnah(أهل سُّنة) have two opinions regarding whether

698
00:48:08,208 --> 00:48:14,272
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ as a Khalifah(خليفه) implicitly or explicitly.

699
00:48:17,901 --> 00:48:20,902
Some scholars consider all of these Ahadith(احاديث)

700
00:48:21,086 --> 00:48:24,632
to hint to the appointment of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) as Khalifah(خليفه)

701
00:48:24,758 --> 00:48:27,733
and to implicitly imply that.

702
00:48:28,323 --> 00:48:30,905
And this is the opinion of Al-Hasan Al-Basri(ألحسن ألبصري)

703
00:48:30,929 --> 00:48:34,569
and it's also the opinion of Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْبن حنبل).

704
00:48:36,971 --> 00:48:38,320
Now, there are some scholars,

705
00:48:38,360 --> 00:48:46,699
who consider the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to be an explicit appointment by Rasool Allah ﷺ

706
00:48:46,762 --> 00:48:49,937
 because he made him the Imam(اِمَام) in Salah(صلاة), which means that he is the Khalifah(خليفه).

707
00:48:50,771 --> 00:48:54,035
And this is the opinion of Ibn Hazm Az-Zahiri(إبن هزم ألظاهري),

708
00:48:54,351 --> 00:48:57,590
and it's also the opinion of some of the scholars of Ahlul-Hadith(أهل الحديث)

709
00:48:58,196 --> 00:48:59,305
 and their evidence is also

710
00:48:59,329 --> 00:49:00,926
إنْ لَمْ تَجِدِينِي فَأْتي أبَا بَكْرٍ

711
00:49:00,950 --> 00:49:02,946
If you don't find me, then go to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

712
00:49:03,224 --> 00:49:10,004
they consider this to be a clear cut appointment by Rasool Allah ﷺ  of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in the position of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

713
00:49:11,740 --> 00:49:14,403
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه), he comments on this by saying that

714
00:49:15,298 --> 00:49:20,342
Rasool Allah ﷺ has hinted, and implied the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

715
00:49:20,786 --> 00:49:24,752
 without writing it down or explicitly mentioning it.

716
00:49:25,482 --> 00:49:28,034
So Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه), he says it was the Hikma(حكمة) of Allah

717
00:49:28,475 --> 00:49:31,743
that the appointment of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) will not be done through a document

718
00:49:31,768 --> 00:49:34,099
or a will by Rasool Allah ﷺ that is written

719
00:49:34,962 --> 00:49:40,115
because Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says: If it was done through a document

720
00:49:41,049 --> 00:49:44,864
then we would say that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was appointed because of that document.

721
00:49:46,004 --> 00:49:52,027
But the way he is appointed now is through the implications of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

722
00:49:52,070 --> 00:49:55,759
and also through the choice of the Muslims because they gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

723
00:49:56,599 --> 00:50:02,662
So it's combined, and it's stronger and it's also an elevation of the status of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

724
00:50:02,739 --> 00:50:07,660
as if Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) is saying that it is common sense it is the expected thing to do

725
00:50:08,815 --> 00:50:10,769
that it doesn't even need to be written down

726
00:50:11,613 --> 00:50:14,639
it is so obvious and clear that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) should be the Khalifah(خليفه).

727
00:50:14,964 --> 00:50:18,040
There is no need for Rasool Allah ﷺ to write it down in the document.

728
00:50:19,685 --> 00:50:23,302
And that did happen, and there was no dispute on the issue

729
00:50:23,327 --> 00:50:25,937
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was given Baiyah(بَيْعة) by the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

730
00:50:26,069 --> 00:50:28,747
There was a private Baiyah(بَيْعة) and then there was a public Baiyah(بَيْعة) in the Masjid(مسجد),

731
00:50:29,087 --> 00:50:31,071
the private Baiyah(بَيْعة) happened in the Saqeefah(ثقيفة).

732
00:50:31,356 --> 00:50:34,348
And then later on, when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was going to give,

733
00:50:34,372 --> 00:50:36,911
 the first Khut'ba(خطبة) of his, as a Khalifah(خليفه)

734
00:50:37,147 --> 00:50:39,445
the rest of the people came and gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

735
00:50:39,653 --> 00:50:46,842
Now Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) how come he didn't give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

736
00:50:46,908 --> 00:50:50,115
in the Saqeefah(ثقيفة), in the portico of Bannu Sa'adah(بنوسعدة).

737
00:50:51,145 --> 00:50:54,604
The answer is simply because Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was the one,

738
00:50:54,628 --> 00:50:59,301
entrusted with the funeral proceedings of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

739
00:51:00,297 --> 00:51:06,038
He was the closest male family relative of Rasool Allah ﷺ

740
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:11,753
therefore, he was given this responsibility of performing the burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

741
00:51:13,241 --> 00:51:17,572
and the Baiyah(بَيْعة), of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) happened on the same day Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

742
00:51:18,836 --> 00:51:20,498
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away on Monday

743
00:51:20,682 --> 00:51:22,047
they gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة) on Monday.

744
00:51:24,917 --> 00:51:27,786
And that's why Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was late in giving him Baiyah(بَيْعة)

745
00:51:27,811 --> 00:51:31,767
but then in the Masjid(مسجد) Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) called him forth

746
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:34,819
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) came and he did give Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) his Baiyah(بَيْعة),

747
00:51:35,417 --> 00:51:39,009
and all of the stories that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was hiding

748
00:51:39,033 --> 00:51:41,325
and he refused to give Baiyah(بَيْعة) are false.

749
00:51:42,822 --> 00:51:46,143
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) had an excuse, in not being available

750
00:51:46,421 --> 00:51:51,162
on the first day because he was busy with a burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

751
00:51:52,940 --> 00:51:53,979
The statement of Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه):

752
00:51:54,010 --> 00:51:58,327
فلو كانت تعين مما يشتبع الأمة لو بين له رسول الله صلى الله بيان القطعًا للعزر

753
00:51:58,651 --> 00:52:01,878
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says: If this was an issue of confusion

754
00:52:02,132 --> 00:52:05,128
Rasool Allah ﷺ would have told the Ummah(امة), what to do would have written it down

755
00:52:05,647 --> 00:52:07,304
but he says it's not an issue of confusion.

756
00:52:08,441 --> 00:52:11,064
The status of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is so high, it's not confusing

757
00:52:11,536 --> 00:52:12,522
he is the Khalifah(خليفه).

758
00:52:15,355 --> 00:52:20,198
Ahlus Sunnah Wal-Jama'ah(أهل سنةوالجماعة) considered to be the consensus of the Sahabah(صحابه).

759
00:52:21,642 --> 00:52:23,343
That Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was the Khalifah(خليفه).

760
00:52:24,902 --> 00:52:26,258
Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد) was asked:

761
00:52:26,282 --> 00:52:27,675
متی بوع یا علی ابي بكر؟

762
00:52:27,699 --> 00:52:29,537
When was the Baiyah(بَيْعة) given to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

763
00:52:29,936 --> 00:52:33,783
He said: The same day Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, because

764
00:52:33,944 --> 00:52:36,834
كره أن يبقه بعديومٍ وليس في جماعة

765
00:52:36,858 --> 00:52:40,767
Because the Sahabah(صحابه) did not want to stay for even one day without a Jama'ah(جماعة).

766
00:52:41,943 --> 00:52:45,736
So they did it the same day Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, even before he was buried.

767
00:52:46,795 --> 00:52:50,620
You know, when we talk about the importance of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

768
00:52:53,218 --> 00:52:58,465
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away and you had the washing of Rasool Allah ﷺ

769
00:52:58,489 --> 00:53:03,331
and burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ and we know that the Sunnah(سنة) is to burry a person as fast as possible.

770
00:53:05,180 --> 00:53:08,247
The burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ ended up being delayed.

771
00:53:08,853 --> 00:53:12,247
He died on Monday and they say that he was buried Wednesday night.

772
00:53:14,345 --> 00:53:22,294
According to some scholars, because the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم wanted to sort out the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) first.

773
00:53:23,182 --> 00:53:28,556
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم who were before that, before the Da'wah(دعوة) of Muhammadﷺ

774
00:53:28,912 --> 00:53:33,249
were the Arab people who were an unruly people, tribes fighting each other

775
00:53:33,604 --> 00:53:37,079
very independent, they do not want to submit to any leader

776
00:53:37,669 --> 00:53:41,324
but now this collective work was so ingrained in them

777
00:53:41,719 --> 00:53:46,960
that they considered it to be, not appropriate for them to stay even for a day

778
00:53:47,237 --> 00:53:50,028
without having an Ameer(أمير), who would run their affairs.

779
00:53:52,493 --> 00:53:56,985
And they gave that precedence over washing Rasool Allah ﷺ, and burying him.

780
00:53:59,174 --> 00:54:02,436
And they were discussing this issue even though their hearts were broken

781
00:54:03,480 --> 00:54:05,433
 because of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ

782
00:54:05,687 --> 00:54:08,540
they were discussing it the same day, and passed away.

783
00:54:10,794 --> 00:54:14,129
And that shows you the importance of the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) in our life

784
00:54:15,476 --> 00:54:21,460
and the Muslims being in a Jama'at(جماعة),  and somebody being in the position of leadership to run and manage their affairs.

785
00:54:23,107 --> 00:54:25,816
So it's iJma'ah(إجماع), of the scholars.

786
00:54:27,276 --> 00:54:28,382
Al-Ba-qallani(ألبا قلاني) says:

787
00:54:28,406 --> 00:54:31,616
وكان رضي الله عنه مفروض طاعة لإجماع المسلمين على طاعة

788
00:54:31,784 --> 00:54:34,918
It was the Ijmah(إجماع) of the Muslims to obey Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

789
00:54:35,555 --> 00:54:37,816
Now the issue of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) and Khalifah(خليفه) again

790
00:54:38,266 --> 00:54:42,347
Al-Imam Al-Marwardi(ألإمام ألمروردي), who's considered to be one of the greatest scholars

791
00:54:42,802 --> 00:54:47,234
of Islam, the classical scholars of Islam in political issues.

792
00:54:48,051 --> 00:54:52,983
He wrote a book called Al-Ahkaam Al-Sultaniya(ألإحكام السلطانية), the laws of governance.

793
00:54:53,878 --> 00:54:54,633
He says;

794
00:54:55,535 --> 00:55:00,046
 فكانت الإمامة أصلًى عليه إستقرد قواعد المِلَّةْ

795
00:55:00,293 --> 00:55:02,892
The issue of having an Imam(اِمَام) and Imam(اِمَام) means, leader,

796
00:55:03,411 --> 00:55:05,724
was one of the fundamentals of the religion.

797
00:55:06,224 --> 00:55:06,921
and he says:

798
00:55:07,018 --> 00:55:13,950
إنَّ الله جلت قدرته’ ندب الأمة زعيمًا خلف به نبوة و حاطبه الملة

799
00:55:14,322 --> 00:55:19,506
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wanted the Ummah(امة) to have a leader, who would succeed the Prophethood.

800
00:55:20,455 --> 00:55:25,154
So the position of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is so important that he is the successor of Prophethood

801
00:55:25,571 --> 00:55:31,407
and he is the one, who fulfills the role that the Prophet used to fulfill, in his life.

802
00:55:32,161 --> 00:55:36,243
 And that's why Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was called Khalifat Rasool Ullah(خليفة الرسول الله).

803
00:55:36,751 --> 00:55:39,650
 The successor of Rasool Allah ﷺ

804
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:41,690
إنْ لَمْ تَجِدِينِي فَأْتي أبَا بَكْرٍ

805
00:55:41,937 --> 00:55:44,175
If you don't find me, then go to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

806
00:55:44,562 --> 00:55:46,860
He was the deputy of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

807
00:55:48,653 --> 00:55:50,279
What is the Hukum(حكم) of Khilafah(خِلَافَه)?

808
00:55:50,954 --> 00:55:51,651
Is it Sunnah(سنة)?

809
00:55:51,744 --> 00:55:52,637
is it the Mubah(مباح)?

810
00:55:52,740 --> 00:55:53,273
is it Wajib(واجب).?

811
00:55:53,335 --> 00:55:54,407
What is Hukum(حكم) of it.?

812
00:55:55,385 --> 00:56:01,860
Ibn Hajr Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني), he comments on the statement made by one scholar, his name is Daudi(داؤدي)

813
00:56:02,799 --> 00:56:05,139
that establishing Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is Sunnah Muakkidah(سنة موكدة).

814
00:56:06,104 --> 00:56:08,046
So Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) responds to that.

815
00:56:08,189 --> 00:56:13,619
 Now the evidence that Ad-Daudi(ألداؤدي) uses is the fact that

816
00:56:14,826 --> 00:56:19,096
the Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) wasn't given until hours after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

817
00:56:19,136 --> 00:56:22,531
 So he said: Since they stayed for a few hours without a Khalifah(خليفه).

818
00:56:22,785 --> 00:56:24,387
It means that it is Sunnah Muakkidah(سنة موكدة).

819
00:56:24,946 --> 00:56:28,038
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني) comments on that and he says;

820
00:56:28,704 --> 00:56:39,863
وَتُعقِبَةْ بالإتفاق على فرضيتها باَنَّهم تراكو لِاَجل إقَامَتَهَا اعظم المحمات وتشاغل بدفن النبي ﷺ

821
00:56:39,888 --> 00:56:47,217
حتى فرغُ منهَا ومدة مزكور زمنًا يسير في بعد يومًا يُغتفرُو مثله لِإجماع الكلمة

822
00:56:48,222 --> 00:56:50,810
He says: But that is not the view of the scholars

823
00:56:51,072 --> 00:56:54,435
the view of the scholars, and it is their consensus, Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) says:

824
00:56:54,459 --> 00:56:57,647
Their consensus that it is mandatory that it is Fardh(فرض).

825
00:56:58,191 --> 00:57:03,531
And to say that because they waited for a few hours, he said;

826
00:57:04,395 --> 00:57:09,753
Waiting for a few hours to bring together the unity among the Muslims is acceptable.

827
00:57:11,499 --> 00:57:15,999
 If waiting for a few hours is going to bring the Ummah(امة) together and unify them, it's acceptable.

828
00:57:16,681 --> 00:57:22,033
And this is the fastest possible time, they could establish the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) within a few hours.

829
00:57:22,368 --> 00:57:26,497
But Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني) makes it very clear that it is Fardh(فرض).

830
00:57:28,705 --> 00:57:33,502
And it is the consensus of the Sahabah(صحابه) because they did it before they even buried Rasool Allah ﷺ.

831
00:57:35,711 --> 00:57:40,208
We sometimes establish our religious views

832
00:57:40,947 --> 00:57:45,536
based on what is the predominant case around us.

833
00:57:46,586 --> 00:57:51,372
So we think, because this is how we are now, this is the right way to be

834
00:57:52,188 --> 00:57:57,233
there are some people now, because there is no Imarah(عمارة) and Khilafah(خِلَافَه) in Islam today

835
00:57:57,618 --> 00:58:00,672
they think that it's absolutely fine and there's no problem in that.

836
00:58:01,630 --> 00:58:06,724
Brothers and Sisters, if one of the Sahabah(صحابه) was alive today they would ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to take away their soul.

837
00:58:07,547 --> 00:58:12,536
They would refuse to live the life that many Muslims are happy to lead today

838
00:58:13,372 --> 00:58:15,980
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم when they were in Makkah

839
00:58:16,005 --> 00:58:21,594
when the Da'wah(دعوة) was starting, and there was only 38 Muslims on the face of the earth.

840
00:58:22,301 --> 00:58:24,904
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

841
00:58:25,080 --> 00:58:28,362
It shouldn't be a secret Da'wah(دعوة), we have to make it public.

842
00:58:29,827 --> 00:58:33,092
And as soon as the Sahabah(صحابه) reached over 100

843
00:58:33,440 --> 00:58:37,899
Rasool Allah ﷺ was now starting for our base to establish his government

844
00:58:38,280 --> 00:58:39,291
and move to Madina

845
00:58:39,523 --> 00:58:43,093
he could have continued staying in Makkah he was protected by his uncle Al-Abbas(العباس).

846
00:58:43,339 --> 00:58:46,310
Rasool Allah ﷺ was not being harmed physically.

847
00:58:47,579 --> 00:58:51,870
Yes, there were threats against his life, but his Da'wah(دعوة) was going on

848
00:58:52,335 --> 00:58:56,837
but Rasool Allah ﷺ for the last few years of his Da'wah(دعوة) in Makkah

849
00:58:57,162 --> 00:58:59,534
was asking for Nusrah(نصرة), asking for support.

850
00:59:00,781 --> 00:59:05,915
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, they couldn't stand seeing Islam being humiliated

851
00:59:05,939 --> 00:59:08,698
they couldn't stand seeing the Muslims being humiliated.

852
00:59:09,210 --> 00:59:13,641
And now this is something perfectly normal and acceptable to some Muslims.

853
00:59:14,582 --> 00:59:18,233
This is not a way of life that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would be happy with.

854
00:59:18,471 --> 00:59:21,294
It's not even a way of life that they would be willing to live

855
00:59:22,411 --> 00:59:25,342
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away and they didn't bury him yet

856
00:59:25,366 --> 00:59:29,647
and they are already meeting to discuss the issue of appointing a Khalifah(خليفه) among them.

857
00:59:30,184 --> 00:59:34,163
I mean, do you understand the implications of that how important they viewed this issue.

858
00:59:35,316 --> 00:59:39,649
 And as the Muslim Ummah(امة) we'll continue suffering setbacks and problems

859
00:59:39,917 --> 00:59:41,828
as long as we don't sort out this issue.

860
00:59:42,551 --> 00:59:45,231
Look at how many family problems exist in the society

861
00:59:45,556 --> 00:59:47,657
among the Muslims, I'm not talking about the non Muslims.

862
00:59:48,145 --> 00:59:50,298
How many family problems are going around

863
00:59:51,739 --> 00:59:53,643
how many financial problems are going around

864
00:59:53,668 --> 00:59:58,755
and when I say finance problems, a person could be a millionaire but they're going to have financial problems,

865
00:59:59,026 --> 01:00:00,640
 because the Rizq(رزق) is coming from Haram(حرام).

866
01:00:02,027 --> 01:00:04,262
How pure is the Rizq(رزق) that Muslims are making?

867
01:00:05,370 --> 01:00:08,027
All of these are issues that cannot be sorted out.

868
01:00:08,563 --> 01:00:13,623
Unless we establish this system, for example, take the issue of mortgage.

869
01:00:14,198 --> 01:00:16,518
There is debate some say Haram(حرام), some say Halal(حلال).

870
01:00:17,522 --> 01:00:19,811
You're damned if you do, you're damned if you don't

871
01:00:20,401 --> 01:00:23,987
if you deal with mortgage, you're dealing with something that is Haram(حرام), Ribaa(رباء).

872
01:00:24,343 --> 01:00:27,383
And if you stay away from it, then you're paying more in rent.

873
01:00:29,606 --> 01:00:32,730
And Muslims want a magical solution for these problems.

874
01:00:33,343 --> 01:00:35,831
There is not going to be any solution

875
01:00:35,855 --> 01:00:38,959
until you bring back the law of Allah, the Hukm(حكم) of Allah in your life.

876
01:00:39,494 --> 01:00:43,079
We are looking for solutions for family problems

877
01:00:43,280 --> 01:00:46,953
problems between the husband and wife, problems between the children and parents

878
01:00:47,232 --> 01:00:50,878
these are not going to be solved unless we're living under an Islamic system.

879
01:00:51,445 --> 01:00:55,864
The Barakah(بركة) in living is, when it is under the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

880
01:00:56,751 --> 01:01:00,277
The most blessed time in the history of this Ummah(امة)

881
01:01:00,440 --> 01:01:03,546
was when they were living under the Khulafaa(خلفاء) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

882
01:01:04,011 --> 01:01:06,878
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان), Ali(علي), Umar Bin Abdel-Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز).

883
01:01:08,000 --> 01:01:13,593
So, this should be on the minds of everyone to bring back the law and the Hukum(حكم) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

884
01:01:13,822 --> 01:01:18,726
And on the other side if anybody thinks that Khilafah(خِلَافَه), can be established

885
01:01:18,964 --> 01:01:20,906
 without the path of Jihad(جهاد) is mistaken.

886
01:01:21,615 --> 01:01:23,876
Because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه says

887
01:01:23,900 --> 01:01:26,665
and we'll talk about his statements in his Khut'ba(خطبة).

888
01:01:27,130 --> 01:01:29,857
وما ترك قوم جهاد في سبيل الله إلَّا ذِلُّ

889
01:01:30,318 --> 01:01:35,649
Any people, who leave the mandate of Jihad(جهاد), are going to be humiliated.

890
01:01:36,403 --> 01:01:38,227
It's the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, it's going to happen.

891
01:01:41,925 --> 01:01:48,240
Some lessons to that could be derived from the meeting in the portico of Sa'adah(سعدة) is,

892
01:01:49,049 --> 01:01:51,386
 Number one, Shura(شورى) in Islam.

893
01:01:52,944 --> 01:01:54,998
There's a narration, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) says;

894
01:01:55,471 --> 01:02:00,330
من دوعيَّ إلى عمارة من غير مشورى  فلا يحلُّ له أن يقبل

895
01:02:00,974 --> 01:02:05,349
Whoever is asked to be in a position of leadership

896
01:02:05,985 --> 01:02:10,062
without the Shura(شورى) of the Muslims, it is not Halal(حلال) for him to accept it.

897
01:02:11,488 --> 01:02:16,156
If you are told come and be Ameer(أمير), and it's without the Shura(شورى) of the Muslims

898
01:02:16,488 --> 01:02:19,951
don't get your feet into that pit hole.

899
01:02:20,893 --> 01:02:23,552
Because Al-Imarah(ألعمارة) is Mas'ooliyah(مسئولية)

900
01:02:23,577 --> 01:02:25,135
and you're going to be asked about, on the Day of Judgment.

901
01:02:25,160 --> 01:02:29,121
And if it's without the Shura(شورى), of the Muslims, you should not accept it.

902
01:02:29,969 --> 01:02:32,448
The Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was to the Shura(شورى) of the Muslims.

903
01:02:32,608 --> 01:02:35,586
Same thing with the khulafah(خلفاء) after that

904
01:02:35,702 --> 01:02:40,802
so we also learned that the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is established through Baiyah(بَيْعة)

905
01:02:42,552 --> 01:02:44,691
and Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث),

906
01:02:44,715 --> 01:02:48,181
 ومن مات وليس في عنقه بيعة مات ميتة جاهلية

907
01:02:48,206 --> 01:02:53,598
If you die, without a pledge of allegiance to the Imam(اِمَام) you are dying in a state of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

908
01:02:53,642 --> 01:02:56,172
Now this is strictly speaking about the Khalifah(خليفه) too.

909
01:02:57,043 --> 01:03:01,123
This is not talking about presidents and kings or local leaders,

910
01:03:01,148 --> 01:03:03,700
it's talking about the Khalifah(خليفه), the Baiyah(بَيْعة).

911
01:03:03,900 --> 01:03:09,382
Al-Baiyah Al-Uzma(ألبَيْعة العظمى) this Baiyah(بَيْعة) that Rasool Allah ﷺ is referring to is about Al-Khilafah (خِلَافَه)

912
01:03:10,530 --> 01:03:12,657
and since there is no Khilafah(خِلَافَه) now.

913
01:03:12,943 --> 01:03:15,948
Then we are living in an exception of this rule

914
01:03:16,069 --> 01:03:20,502
until the Khalifah(خليفه) exists, then the Hadith(حديث) would apply again.

915
01:03:20,983 --> 01:03:28,037
Also, we learn that the issue of bringing up Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

916
01:03:28,061 --> 01:03:33,728
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه bringing up Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)  is because it's a practical issue, it's a realistic issue

917
01:03:33,799 --> 01:03:38,433
 and this needs to be taken into consideration in Islamic work.

918
01:03:39,009 --> 01:03:40,663
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is saying;

919
01:03:40,791 --> 01:03:45,708
The nature of the Arabs is that they wouldn't accept a leader from outside Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

920
01:03:46,174 --> 01:03:50,468
so one needs to take into consideration, the nature of the people

921
01:03:51,043 --> 01:03:55,393
one needs to take into consideration, what is possible and what is not possible

922
01:03:55,858 --> 01:04:02,535
and not try to be idealistic and unrealistic in their affairs and in their Da'wah(دعوة).

923
01:04:04,351 --> 01:04:08,144
This is beyond the scope of these talks on Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

924
01:04:08,703 --> 01:04:12,482
But Ibn Khaldoon(إبن خلدون) has a lot to say about this issue of how come Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

925
01:04:13,119 --> 01:04:16,226
and he talks about the issue of Usbah(عصبة) the strength

926
01:04:16,766 --> 01:04:18,658
and the support that is given by the tribe

927
01:04:19,092 --> 01:04:20,990
he talks about that in his book Al-Muqaddimah(ألمقدمه).

928
01:04:23,154 --> 01:04:26,384
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

